                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Underwhelming is an understatement.  \n\nIt's free, but still probably not worth the effort.  Unless I'm missing something, there are only two fireworks.. both are less than impressive.  The best part was when I lit the fireworks stash with the match and a bunch went off at once.\n\nEver since I shot off the fireworks in Call of the Starseed I've hoped for a strictly fireworks VR experience.  This is a long shot from even what I'd hope for at a minimum.  More fireworks, better detailed environment, color/aura changes, etc.  Even Pierhead Arcade has more impressive fireworks in it's prize shack when you turn in tickets.  \n\nThis isn't something I'd demo VR with.. it might be suitable for a toddler, but even their attention span will push it off after a few minutes.",
